A||N||7||Earne||BAM-BAM, You've Got Pics!||||1||
Z||000000||Earne||03-15-2000||06:11 AM||||Here are a few more pics of my Toy.  The weather keeps playin' with us here, 75 degrees, 3" of snow, this was a good day but only about 50 degrees.  I'm looking forward to better weather so I can get the Toy to Bob Stieger in Illinois for the T-Top installation.  Anyway, here goes.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828278&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828278&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828308&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828308&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828309&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828309&Sequence=2</A> <P><BR>There was a thread here about scoops.  I mentioned that no replacement scoop panel fits like the original.  These were added to the original panel.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828288&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828288&Sequence=2</A> <P><BR>I added a few new pieces to the engine, EGR valve, oil &tranny stick and tranny tube, trans cable bracket.  Still waitin' for the deck lid hinges and heat shield for the tranny cable.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828298&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828298&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828302&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828302&Sequence=2</A> <P><BR>I'm not happy with the MSD coil I added.  Just doesn't "look" right.  Any suggestions?<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828303&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828303&Sequence=2</A> <P><BR>Here is a shot of under the hood.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828305&Sequence=3" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828305&Sequence=3</A> <P><BR>Here are the interior shots you wanted.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828282&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828282&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828281&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828281&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828290&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828290&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828294&Sequence=4" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828294&Sequence=4</A> <P><BR>Here is a shot of the mirror from a '98-'99 Cadilac.  Couldn't find one in a Pontiac.  All the interior lights (except two outside maps) were changed to red to match dash lighting.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828291&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828291&Sequence=2</A> <P><BR>Here is a little something I picked up last year for this years shows.  Always too much sun and heat in the parking lot shows.  Maybe it will help, at least it's worth a grin and it converts to a bicycle rack, too.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828283&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828283&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828285&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828285&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828287&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828287&Sequence=2</A> <P><BR>All are welcome to the Fiero Fest 2000 June 16, 17, and 18 in Farmington Hills, Michigan.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828293&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=756835&p=17828293&Sequence=2</A> <P><BR>Hope these are what you were looking for.<p>[This message has been edited by Earne (edited 12-31-1995).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||03-15-2000||08:34 AM||||Wow.  I've seen some nice Fieros.  We all have.  But I think yours captures the high-dollar, high-class exotic look better than any Fiero I've ever seen.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Bill Osmer||03-15-2000||12:39 PM||||Earne -<P>Great job!!!!<P>And I especially like the fact that you did all this to a silver GT... You guessed it - I have a silver GT, too.<P>However, now I'm concerned about going to the Farmington Hills Fiero Fest - you'll by far out class me!!!||||reg||4
Z||000003||DRH||03-15-2000||03:28 PM||||Nice Car!!!<P>Idea on the coil... I never liked having the coil directly above the exhaust. Maybe move it somewhere less visible??? Don't know if that's practical... just an idea...<P>I <B>really</B> like the interior. Updated, but not totally different. Kinda like what GM "shoulda" done.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||03-15-2000||08:41 PM||||  Earne, Thanks man, that looks great!. I really want to takl to PISA about the dash. Did you order that on-line or was it in the "BIG BOOK"? let me know. Again, thanks. My son is almost convinced; when he comes home after spring ball(NCAA Football) he wants to talk Fiero's <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">. I think I successfully pulled him away from the ECLIPSE. Take care and be cool!<P>  Thanx, BAM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||03-15-2000||09:12 PM||||Earne, are the scoops an add on to the original panel? If so where did you get them? Sounds like an easier/cheaper way to get scooped. I gotta have some scoops  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||doughboySE||03-15-2000||10:01 PM||||HEY IS IT JUST ME OR DOES THAT PAINT FLIP FLOP LIKE MINE <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>MINE FLOPS FROM GOLD TO VIOLET TO WHITE<BR>THAT LOOKS LIKE IT FLIPS VIOLET AS WELL||||reg||1
Z||000007||Earne||03-15-2000||10:33 PM||||Thanks all, it means a lot more to receive praise from this group.<P>BAM-BAM:  I found it in the Big Book.  Then I called PISA and dealt with them directly.  They sent me a sample leather book on the promise that I would mail it back to them after I decided, I did.  Gave me credit for the aftermarket glovebox I already had.  $650  Great people to deal with.<P>SCCA FIERO:  The scoops are patterned after the Mecham in size, and the original Pontiac design (no strakes), but different from both.  They fill the entire panel down to the GT ground effects.  I bought FOCOA's, sent them back, bought from FieroHeaven, sent them back.  Ended up making my own.  The bottom angle of the scoops and the panel fit wasn't acceptable.  I ended up making my own from fiberglass and used 3M structural plastic adhesive to bond to body panel.  The same kind of stuff the hood and deck lid pieces are bonded with.  Then I cut out the back of the panel to be functional.  Molded to panel with plastic filler.  I also cut the insulation panel outboard of the battery.  Many people don't know there is already a port in the metal there, just covered with insulation.  Now both sides are functional.  If it sounds like the long way round, it is.  But I think the result is worth it.  I just saw a pic of FOCOA's new P2000 scoops, they look like mine.  I wish FieroPhil would like my idea about the '89 GT front facia enough to produce it and save me a lot of work.||||reg||1
